                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "cinemag":</h3><p><img src="http://recordinghacks.com/images/logos/logo_cinemag.gif" class="shaft thumb" width="125" height="72" /><b>CineMag</b> is a US-based manufacturer of audio transformers. The company was founded in 1979 by Tom Reichenbach.</p><p>CineMag provides transformers to numerous mic and preamp manufacturers, including AEA, Groove Tubes, Bock Audio, Cloud, Avant, Tonelux, and Universal Audio (to name a few).</p><p>Mic output transformers from CineMag are widely used to upgrade inexpensive imported microphones, whose stock transformers often restrict the performance of the rest of the amplifier circuitry.</p>
